  2. The picture, Template_MiSTer's TV static (rtl/mycore.v, rtl/lfsr.v), re-implemented as clocked logic on the
     framework's beam; these lines follow theirs:
       rtl/tango_core_template.v                                      Template_MiSTer
       393  wire [5:0] rnd_c = {r[0], r[1], r[2], r[2], r[2], r[2]};   rtl/mycore.v 26 (the same bits of rnd_reg)
       392  wire [5:0] cos_g = {1'b0, cosv[7:3]} + 6'd32;              rtl/mycore.v 85
       394  wire [7:0] video = (cos_g >= rnd_c) ?                       rtl/mycore.v 88 (the same expression)
                               {cos_g - rnd_c, 2'b00} : 8'd0;
       388  wire [9:0] cph = vvc + {cl, 2'b00};                         rtl/mycore.v 86 (the cosine's argument)
       385-386  vvc cleared by reset, stepped by 6 each frame           rtl/mycore.v 55, 44 (the step of 5 for PAL is
                                                                      the Tango authors')
       366  wire fb = ~(r[62] ^ r[60] ^ r[59] ^ r[57] ^ r[53]);         rtl/lfsr.v 8 (the 63-bit LFSR's taps N-1, N-3,
                                                                      N-4, N-6, N-10; there a free-running ring of
                                                                      lcells, here a clocked register, line 370)
     Template_MiSTer's cosine table (rtl/cos.sv) is not used: rtl/template_cos.vh is computed by tools/gen_cos.py,
     q[i] = round(127 cos((i + 0.5) pi / 512)).

